# Source always diffs as text.
#
# A single stray NUL byte in a source file (starred/starredStore.ts had one in
# a template literal) makes git call the whole file binary: no diff in review,
# no blame, no `git log -p`, and grep skips it. The `diff` attribute forces the
# textual diff for these paths even when such a byte slips in again. It does
# not touch EOL handling — that stays at git's default.
*.ts    diff
*.tsx   diff
*.vue   diff
*.js    diff
*.json  diff
*.css   diff
*.md    diff
